{"page_content": "Generation of new non-animal data c\n\nNote: Section 8.3.1 of Annex VII to the REACH Regulation specifies that when new information needs to be generated testing must start with in chemico/in vitro methods. Before performing in chemico/in vitro testing, it is important to consider whether the test method(s) to be used are suitable for the substance i.e. whether the substance fits in the applicability domain of a specific test method. In case the in chemico/in vitro tests are not suitable for the substance, an LLNA would need to be performed, as specified in Annex VII, section 8.3.2.", "metadata": {"doc_id": "1fd0b333-c50a-4fa5-9e21-e2f8d78ab55c", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "information_requirements_r7a_en.pdf"}}